---
/**
 * Book I, Ch. XIII, Prop. 3: the same draw, written two ways. On the left the
 * draw sits on the path from the parameters to the loss and blocks the chain
 * rule. On the right the randomness enters from the side and the path is a
 * sum and a product.
 */
---
<svg class="fig" viewBox="0 0 440 320" role="img" aria-labelledby="rp-t rp-d" style="--fig-min: 0px">
  <title id="rp-t">Sampling on the path, and sampling beside it</title>
  <desc id="rp-d">
    Two small graphs. On the left, mu and sigma feed a sampling node that
    draws z from a normal distribution, and z feeds the function f. The
    backward arrow from f to mu and sigma is crossed out, because a draw has no
    derivative with respect to its parameters. On the right, epsilon is drawn
    from a standard normal outside the path, and z is computed as mu plus sigma
    times epsilon, so the derivatives are one with respect to mu and epsilon
    with respect to sigma.
  </desc>

  <text x="8" y="23" class="t-lab">draw on the path</text>
  <text x="232" y="23" class="t-lab">draw beside it</text>
  <line x1="220" y1="40" x2="220" y2="262" class="wire-soft" />

  <rect x="20" y="60" width="44" height="28" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="42" y="79" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">μ</text>
  <rect x="140" y="60" width="44" height="28" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="162" y="79" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">σ</text>
  <line x1="42" y1="88" x2="96" y2="126" class="wire" />
  <line x1="162" y1="88" x2="108" y2="126" class="wire" />
  <rect x="50" y="128" width="104" height="40" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="102" y="146" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">draw z</text>
  <text x="102" y="161" class="t-sm" text-anchor="middle">~ N(μ, σ²)</text>
  <line x1="102" y1="168" x2="102" y2="196" class="wire" />
  <polygon points="97,196 102,206 107,196" class="head" />
  <rect x="80" y="208" width="44" height="28" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="102" y="227" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">f(z)</text>
  <path d="M 130 222 C 196 200 196 120 168 96" class="dash" />
  <line x1="176" y1="150" x2="196" y2="170" class="s2" stroke-width="2" />
  <line x1="196" y1="150" x2="176" y2="170" class="s2" stroke-width="2" />
  <text x="20" y="258" class="t-sm">no derivative through a draw</text>

  <rect x="240" y="60" width="44" height="28" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="262" y="79" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">μ</text>
  <rect x="314" y="60" width="44" height="28" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="336" y="79" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">σ</text>
  <circle cx="404" cy="74" r="16" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="404" y="79" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">ε</text>
  <text x="404" y="106" class="t-sm" text-anchor="middle">~ N(0, 1)</text>
  <circle cx="370" cy="140" r="13" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="370" y="145" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">×</text>
  <line x1="336" y1="88" x2="362" y2="129" class="wire" />
  <line x1="398" y1="112" x2="380" y2="130" class="wire" />
  <circle cx="300" cy="170" r="13" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="300" y="175" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">+</text>
  <line x1="262" y1="88" x2="294" y2="158" class="wire" />
  <line x1="358" y1="146" x2="312" y2="164" class="wire" />
  <line x1="300" y1="183" x2="300" y2="196" class="wire" />
  <polygon points="295,196 300,206 305,196" class="head" />
  <rect x="278" y="208" width="44" height="28" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="300" y="227" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">f(z)</text>
  <text x="232" y="258" class="t-sm">∂z/∂μ = 1, ∂z/∂σ = ε</text>

  <text x="8" y="290" class="t-sm">Both draw z from N(μ, σ²). Only the right one</text>
  <text x="8" y="309" class="t-sm">lets the chain rule reach μ and σ.</text>
</svg>
